[69.78123, "o", "\r\u001b[2KNext I’ll check available Ubuntu packages and network access; this determines whether STP/KLEE can be installed natively or must be built from source.\r\n\r\n```\r\nbash -lc '\r\necho \"== apt policy ==\"\r\napt-cache policy klee stp libstp-dev llvm-16-dev libboost-all-dev 2>/dev/null | sed -n \"1,160p\"\r\necho \"== installed dev deps ==\"\r\ndpkg -l | grep -E \"llvm-16|clang-16|boost|stp|minisat|z3|gtest|cmake|ninja|libcap|ncurses\" | head -100\r\necho \"== network ==\"\r\ntimeout 20 git ls-remote --heads https://github.com/klee/klee.git 2>&1 | head -5\r\n'\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠹\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
