[144.931429, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m12\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠹\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[144.932467, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe system MiniSat defines `l_True`/`l_Undef` as macros, which conflicts with STP’s qualified casts. I’ll apply a minimal compatibility patch and resume the STP\r\nbuild.\r\n\r\n```\r\nbash -lc '\r\nset -e\r\nsed -i -E \"s/\\(Minisat::lbool\\)Minisat::l_(True|False|Undef)/(Minisat::lbool)l_\\1/g\" /tmp/stp-src/lib/Sat/MinisatCore.cpp \r\n/tmp/stp-src/lib/Sat/SimplifyingMinisat.cpp\r\ngrep -R \"Minisat::l_\\(True\\|False\\|Undef\\)\" -n /tmp/stp-src/lib/Sat || true\r\ncmake --build /tmp/stp-build -j\"$(nproc)\" 2>&1 | tee /tmp/stp-build2.log\r\ncmake --install /tmp/stp-build 2>&1 | tee /tmp/stp-install2.log\r\nldconfig\r\necho \"== stp checks ==\"\r\ncommand -v stp\r\nstp --version 2>&1 | head -10\r\nls -l /usr/local/lib/libstp* /usr/local/include/stp/c_interface.h /usr/local/lib/cmake/STP/STPConfig.cmake 2>/dev/null\r\n'\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠹\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[144.93264, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠹\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
