[232.040413, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m22\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠋\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[232.04169, "o", "\r\u001b[2KI’ll insert the environment exports before Ubuntu’s non-interactive guard so they work when `~/.bashrc` is sourced by tests, then run an end-to-end symbolic \r\nexecution using the installed command and header.\r\n\r\n```\r\nbash -lc '\r\nset -e\r\ncat > /tmp/klee_env.sh <<\"EOF\"\r\n\r\n# KLEE environment (LLVM 16 + STP)\r\nexport PATH=\"/usr/local/bin:$PATH\"\r\nexport CPATH=\"/usr/local/include${CPATH:+:$CPATH}\"\r\nexport LD_LIBRARY_PATH=\"/usr/local/lib${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH}\"\r\nEOF\r\nif ! grep -q \"KLEE environment\" ~/.bashrc; then\r\n  sed -i \"3r /tmp/klee_env.sh\" ~/.bashrc\r\nfi\r\necho \"== top of bashrc ==\"\r\nnl -ba ~/.bashrc | sed -n \"1,20p\"\r\necho \"== source test ==\"\r\nenv -i HOME=/root PATH=/usr/bin:/bin bash --noprofile --norc -c \"source ~/.bashrc; echo PATH=\\$PATH; echo CPATH=\\$CPATH; echo LD_LIBRARY_PATH=\\$LD_LIBRARY_PATH;\r\ncommand -v klee; test -r /usr/local/include/klee/klee.h && echo HEADER_OK\"\r\n'\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠋\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[232.042059, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠋\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[232.059811, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
[232.060581, "o", "<returncode>\r\n0\r\n<output>\r\n== top of bashrc ==\r\n     1  # ~/.bashrc: executed by bash(1) for non-login shells.\r\n     2  # see /usr/share/doc/bash/examples/startup-files (in the package bash-doc)\r\n     3  # for examples\r\n     4  \r\n     5  # KLEE environment (LLVM 16 + STP)\r\n     6  export PATH=\"/usr/local/bin:$PATH\"\r\n     7  export CPATH=\"/usr/local/include${CPATH:+:$CPATH}\"\r\n     8  export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=\"/usr/local/lib${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH}\"\r\n     9  \r\n    10  # If not running interactively, don't do anything\r\n    11  [ -z \"$PS1\" ] && return\r\n    12  \r\n    13  # don't put duplicate lines in the history. See bash(1) for more options\r\n    14  # ... or force ignoredups and ignorespace\r\n    15  HISTCONTROL=ignoredups:ignorespace\r\n    16  \r\n    17  # append to the history file, don't overwrite it\r\n    18  shopt -s histappend\r\n    19  \r\n    20  # for setting history length see HISTSIZE and HISTFILESIZE in bash(1)\r\n== source test ==\r\nPATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin\r\nCPATH=/usr/local/include\r\nLD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/local/lib\r\n/usr/local/bin/klee\r\nHEADER_OK\r\n\r\n"]
[232.064705, "o", "\u001b[92m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[?25l"]
