[236.828696, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe environment loads correctly in a non-interactive shell. I’ll now compile a C program using `<klee/klee.h>` through `CPATH` and execute it under KLEE to \r\nconfirm the complete installation works.\r\n\r\n```\r\nbash -lc '\r\nset -e\r\nsource ~/.bashrc\r\ncat > /tmp/klee_smoke.c <<\"EOF\"\r\n#include <klee/klee.h>\r\n#include <assert.h>\r\n\r\nint main(void) {\r\n  int x;\r\n  klee_make_symbolic(&x, sizeof(x), \"x\");\r\n  if (x == 42) {\r\n    return 1;\r\n  }\r\n  return 0;\r\n}\r\nEOF\r\nclang-16 -emit-llvm -c -g -O0 /tmp/klee_smoke.c -o /tmp/klee_smoke.bc\r\nrm -rf /tmp/klee_smoke_out\r\ntimeout 120 klee --output-dir=/tmp/klee_smoke_out /tmp/klee_smoke.bc 2>&1 | tee /tmp/klee_smoke_run.log\r\necho \"== generated tests ==\"\r\nfind /tmp/klee_smoke_out -maxdepth 1 -name \"*.ktest\" -printf \"%f\\n\" | sort\r\necho \"== klee info ==\"\r\nklee --version | head -10\r\n'\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠇\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[236.829088, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠇\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
