[276.767303, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m26\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠋\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[276.768013, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe environment is stable and idempotent. I’ll run one final smoke test from a clean sourced shell, then submit.\r\n\r\n```\r\nbash -lc '\r\nset -e\r\nsource ~/.bashrc\r\ncommand -v klee\r\ntest -f \"${CPATH%%:*}/klee/klee.h\"\r\nclang-16 -emit-llvm -c -g -O0 /tmp/klee_smoke.c -o /tmp/klee_final.bc\r\nrm -rf /tmp/klee_final_out\r\ntimeout 120 klee --solver-backend=stp --output-dir=/tmp/klee_final_out /tmp/klee_final.bc 2>&1 | grep -E \"Using STP solver backend|generated tests\"\r\nklee --version | grep -E \"KLEE|LLVM version\"\r\necho \"FINAL_SMOKE_OK\"\r\n'\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠋\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[276.768496, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠋\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[276.84091, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
